1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,267
This video covers the Kefir Hub tools: the file browser, homebrew apps, the App

2
00:00:05,267 --> 00:00:09,200
Store, sysmodules, the fan curve, Wi-Fi and Kefir Settings.

3
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:12,667
For each we show the one or two most useful actions.

4
00:00:12,667 --> 00:00:14,667
Let's start with files.

5
00:00:14,667 --> 00:00:17,000
On the Tools tab open File Browser.

6
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:20,267
A opens a folder or a file, B goes up one folder.

7
00:00:20,267 --> 00:00:23,400
To copy files, mark them with X and press Plus.

8
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:25,400
File Options opens.

9
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:27,600
Choose Copy, or Cut to move them.

10
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:31,467
Go to the destination folder, press Plus and choose Paste.

11
00:00:31,467 --> 00:00:36,533
If a file with the same name is there, Kefir Hub asks whether to replace it.

12
00:00:36,533 --> 00:00:40,733
Press the left stick, L3, and the screen splits into two panes.

13
00:00:40,733 --> 00:00:43,467
D-pad left and right switch between them.

14
00:00:43,467 --> 00:00:48,267
Each pane can show its own source, for example the card and a USB drive.

15
00:00:48,267 --> 00:00:52,800
To delete: mark the files, press Plus, Delete, and confirm with Yes.

16
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:56,600
Careful: there is no recycle bin, deleted files are gone.

17
00:00:56,600 --> 00:01:00,067
A on a zip archive opens it like a read-only folder.

18
00:01:00,067 --> 00:01:04,800
To unpack the whole archive, press Plus, Extract zip, and Extract here.

19
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:06,800
Text files can be edited.

20
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:08,800
Open the file and choose Edit.

21
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:14,133
A changes a line with the keyboard, and Y on a line like enabled = true switches

22
00:01:14,133 --> 00:01:16,133
true and false.

23
00:01:16,133 --> 00:01:18,133
Save with Plus, Save.

24
00:01:18,133 --> 00:01:20,133
Now apps.

25
00:01:20,133 --> 00:01:22,600
L takes you back to the Homebrew tab.

26
00:01:22,600 --> 00:01:25,267
It lists every app in the switch folder.

27
00:01:25,267 --> 00:01:27,267
A launches the selected app.

28
00:01:27,267 --> 00:01:32,000
The right stick, R3, stars an app: it gets a star and stays at the top.

29
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:35,133
Plus opens the options: sort, order and layout.

30
00:01:35,133 --> 00:01:39,400
Install Forwarder adds the app to the HOME Menu as its own icon.

31
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:45,000
Careful: a forwarder is installed like a game, and installing unofficial content can

32
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:47,867
get the console banned when it goes online.

33
00:01:47,867 --> 00:01:50,733
New apps are easiest to get from the store.

34
00:01:50,733 --> 00:01:54,467
On the Tools tab open Software, then Homebrew App Store.

35
00:01:54,467 --> 00:02:00,000
The icon on a tile shows whether the app is installed and whether an update exists.

36
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:02,000
Select an app and press A.

37
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:06,133
On its page choose Install, or Update if a new version is out.

38
00:02:06,133 --> 00:02:08,133
Remove deletes its files.

39
00:02:08,133 --> 00:02:12,467
To find an app by name, press Plus in the list and choose Search.

40
00:02:12,467 --> 00:02:14,467
Next, sysmodules.

41
00:02:14,467 --> 00:02:16,467
Open Tools, Module Manager.

42
00:02:16,467 --> 00:02:20,600
A green dot means the module runs now, grey means it does not.

43
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:24,200
On the right you see whether it starts after a reboot.

44
00:02:24,200 --> 00:02:26,733
A starts or stops the selected module.

45
00:02:26,733 --> 00:02:30,667
Y turns autostart on or off; this applies on the next boot.

46
00:02:30,667 --> 00:02:35,800
Careful: stopping a module the system or a game depends on can make it crash.

47
00:02:35,800 --> 00:02:37,800
Then reboot the console.

48
00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:41,133
Fan curve sets the fan speed for each temperature.

49
00:02:41,133 --> 00:02:45,467
The first time, Kefir Hub offers to install the Kefir fan module.

50
00:02:45,467 --> 00:02:49,200
Choose Install: the curve then applies without a reboot.

51
00:02:49,200 --> 00:02:52,733
X switches between the handheld and the docked curve.

52
00:02:52,733 --> 00:02:57,867
Select a point, press A, and change the temperature and speed with the D-pad.

53
00:02:57,867 --> 00:02:59,933
Plus, Apply, saves both curves.

54
00:02:59,933 --> 00:03:03,200
ZL loads a preset, for example Quiet or Balanced.

55
00:03:03,200 --> 00:03:08,800
Be careful with Fan off: the fan does not spin at any temperature, so watch the heat

56
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:10,800
while you play.

57
00:03:10,800 --> 00:03:13,867
Wi-Fi lists the networks saved on the console.

58
00:03:13,867 --> 00:03:15,933
A connects to the selected one.

59
00:03:15,933 --> 00:03:19,667
New networks are added in the console's System Settings.

60
00:03:19,667 --> 00:03:24,867
Plus on a network opens its actions: Change password, Delete network and more.

61
00:03:24,867 --> 00:03:30,467
View password & details shows the password in plain text, so do not open it in front

62
00:03:30,467 --> 00:03:32,467
of others.

63
00:03:32,467 --> 00:03:35,200
Finally, Kefir Settings on the Tools tab.

64
00:03:35,200 --> 00:03:40,133
These are switches for Kefir and Atmosphère that change files on the card.

65
00:03:40,133 --> 00:03:43,533
The value on the right always shows the real state.

66
00:03:43,533 --> 00:03:45,533
Select a setting and press A.

67
00:03:45,533 --> 00:03:47,533
The box explains what happens.

68
00:03:47,533 --> 00:03:50,867
To confirm, hold A until the bar fills; B cancels.

69
00:03:50,867 --> 00:03:55,533
Most settings reboot the console right away, while USB 3.0 asks first.

70
00:03:55,533 --> 00:04:00,933
Careful: 8GB DRAM status is only for consoles with 8GB of RAM physically soldered

71
00:04:00,933 --> 00:04:02,933
on.

72
00:04:02,933 --> 00:04:05,733
Any other console will not boot correctly.

73
00:04:05,733 --> 00:04:09,933
To undo it, in hekate open Payloads, TegraExplorer, and run the

74
00:04:09,933 --> 00:04:11,933
Remove_8GB-RAM_config script.

75
00:04:11,933 --> 00:04:17,467
Translate Interface replaces one of the console's system languages with a community

76
00:04:17,467 --> 00:04:19,467
translation.

77
00:04:19,467 --> 00:04:24,133
Choose Load translations and hold A to get the list for your firmware.

78
00:04:24,133 --> 00:04:28,333
Select a translation and the language it replaces, then hold A.

79
00:04:28,333 --> 00:04:30,333
The console reboots.

80
00:04:30,333 --> 00:04:35,600
Every firmware install removes the translation, so install it again afterwards.

81
00:04:35,600 --> 00:04:41,067
Read more on the File Browser, Homebrew, Software, System tools and Kefir Settings

82
00:04:41,067 --> 00:04:43,067
pages of the Kefir Hub docs.
